    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP, the priority today is capitalizing on favorable matchups against mid-tier arms, headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who sits atop our projections with a 76.21 efficiency score. Facing Keider Montero and his 4.45 xERA, **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 14% platoon bump and favorable lineup placement, making him our cornerstone play. **James Wood** (61.94) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (61.14) also emerge as core starts; **James Wood** secures his high score through leadoff duties and a strong xwOBA, while **Tyler Soderstrom** leverages a massive 16% park factor enhancement against Kyle Bradish. Meanwhile, we remain aggressive with **Seiya Suzuki** (59.13), whose matchup against Kumar Rocker is bolstered by a 100% stolen base opportunity window against the opposing battery, a critical factor for our roster\u2019s speed-first philosophy.\n\nThe benching process was particularly grueling at the MI slot, where **Kyle Karros** landed just shy of our 40.0 threshold with a 39.67 score. Despite favorable park conditions, his matchup against Jesus Luzardo\u2014a high-efficiency arm\u2014dragged his score down via an 19% SP skill penalty, compounded by an elite catcher pop time that neutralized his potential for stolen bases. Consequently, we are favoring **Brice Turang** and **Cole Young** in the middle infield despite their own matchup volatility. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Austin Riley**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **James Wood** closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status for these starters introduces non-trivial risk; should confirmed lineups shift these players down the order, we may see further dips below the 40-point efficiency floor. Finally, while **Jose Caballero** and **Travis Bazzana** remain on the outside looking in, their proximity to the cut-line confirms that our bench depth remains prepared to rotate in if the matchup environment shifts mid-day.",
